e1000: register the CE4100 MDIO bus from the device tree

The CE4100 GbE has its own MDIO controller, which e1000 uses only for
its built-in PHY handling. A PHY on that bus is invisible to phylib, so
its driver never probes.

If the device's OF node has an "mdio" child, register the bus with the
PHYs it describes. Accesses take the lock e1000's own PHY accesses take.
The bus is unregistered before the MDIO registers are unmapped. Without
the node, nothing changes.

A failed PHY scan now returns -EIO itself, as the bus registration
leaves err cleared.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
